     This is so weird that I couldn't help sending it in. This file is 
simultaneously editaеееееееее JMP, CALL, RET, PUSH, POP, math and logical 
instructions. Here it is in assembly language:

 addr   hex byte ASCII		instrucеееееееее   Many disks have "README" files for info, comments, demos, etc.  
You use the CP/M command "TYPE README" to display them on tеееееееееm
                	;       Lee Hart 11/26/90

 			cr	equ 0dh
 			lf 	equ 0ah
                
 0100           		org 100h	;еееееееее"Is there a way to make 
them into .COM files, so they could be executed as programs?" That 
way, all I'd have to type is "REAеееееееее )    		dad h		; "0" and "1" w/o control codes
 0105  54         T		mov d,h		;   D=1		
 0106  5D         ]		mov e,l		;   E=0
еееееееееk around inside CP/M to 
shorten or eliminate the need for the TYPE command, etc. But most of 
these solutions are more troublеееееееееh		;   B=5
 010B  29         )		dad h
 010C  25         %		dcr h		; create 9
 010D  4C         L		mov c,h		;   C=9 (BDOS "typеееееееееrogram files: it just blindly loads 
anything called ".COM" into memory, and executes it.

     "Execute" is right. If you trеееееееееl
 0113  2D         -		dcr l		; HL=011Eh (addr of JMP opcode)
 0114  3E 3C      ><		mvi a,'<'
 0116  2F         /		cma		; A="еееееееееopcodes. Sensible-looking text becomes a nonsense 
program. But what if I choose ASCII characters that just happen to 
form a еееееееееte "JMP xx05"
 011A  23         #		inx h
 011B  73         s		mov m,e		; write "JMP 0005"
 011C  23         #		inx h
 011D  еееееееее listing is the result. It's 
really a program that types all of the following text, until it finds 
a "dollar" sign. Just useеееееееее
      (C3 05 00)               (jmp 0005) 	;  jump to BDOS "type string" 
 0121                		db  'Normal ASCII text goes еееееееееprogram!

     Writing it was rather restrictive. I wanted the "program" to use 
only printable ASCII characters: no control еееееееееike this is a little like 
putting together a jigsaw puzzle. I wonder if there are any other uses 
for this method. Can we eliеееееееееCMC, STC, HLT, all the MOV opcodes, 
and some of the MVI, INR, DCR, INX, DCX, LXI and DAD instructions. But 
it leaves out allеееееееееble and printable as a text file, and executable 
as a CP/M program (.COM) file. Thanks to that silly looking first line!

  еееееееееtion	comments
 ----   -------- -----          -----------     ---------------------------

                        ;	ascii.asеееееееееhe screen.  
I created a bunch of them to show off one of my programs, but got 
